// Monorepo workspace: each subproject is its own Go module, built
// separately; the only shared code is the proto contract in protocol/
// (clawson.proto + committed generated pb). The workspace exists so go
// commands work from the repo root — most importantly `go run ./daemon
// daemon`, which must run with cwd = repo root because the daemon resolves
// its runtime dirs (groups/, creds/, fcassets/, run/) relative to cwd.
go 1.24.2

use (
	./daemon
	./fcguest
	./protocol
	./tui
)

// Workspace-only fix for an ambiguous-import: gvisor (via the daemon's
// gvisor-tap-vsock dep) requires the pre-split genproto monolith, which
// still ships googleapis/rpc/status — colliding with the split
// genproto/googleapis/rpc module that grpc uses. Module-mode graph pruning
// hides the monolith; the workspace's union graph does not. Pin it to a
// post-split version (2024-02-13, no googleapis/rpc inside) so only the
// split module provides the package. Harmless to module builds (GOWORK=off),
// which never select the monolith at all.
replace google.golang.org/genproto => google.golang.org/genproto v0.0.0-20240213162025-012b6fc9bca9
